{% comment %}
  "Tampa, FL" from a seminar product's city and state metafields.

  Usage -- the caller must CAPTURE it, since a snippet cannot return a value:

    {%- capture place -%}
      {%- render 'suf-seminar-place', product: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign place = place | strip -%}

  ONE SNIPPET BECAUSE TWO PLACES NEED THE SAME STRING -- the event row and the
  bundle's seminar picker. It also ends up on the order, so a picker that said
  "Portland" while the row said "Portland, OR" would be two names for one
  booking.

  THE STATE IS A CHOICE LIST OF FULL NAMES and renders as an abbreviation. The
  merchant picks "Florida" from a dropdown, which is what makes it unmissable
  in the admin; the row shows "FL", because a table cell has no room for
  "Florida" and the abbreviation is what a US reader scans for.

  Falls back to the full name if a value is ever added to the choice list
  without a matching pair below -- a state spelled out is worse-looking than
  the abbreviation, and better than a row with no state at all.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign city = product.metafields.custom.seminar_city.value
  assign state = product.metafields.custom.seminar_state.value
-%}

{%- if state != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign pairs = 'Alabama|AL,Alaska|AK,Arizona|AZ,Arkansas|AR,California|CA,Colorado|CO,Connecticut|CT,Delaware|DE,District of Columbia|DC,Florida|FL,Georgia|GA,Hawaii|HI,Idaho|ID,Illinois|IL,Indiana|IN,Iowa|IA,Kansas|KS,Kentucky|KY,Louisiana|LA,Maine|ME,Maryland|MD,Massachusetts|MA,Michigan|MI,Minnesota|MN,Mississippi|MS,Missouri|MO,Montana|MT,Nebraska|NE,Nevada|NV,New Hampshire|NH,New Jersey|NJ,New Mexico|NM,New York|NY,North Carolina|NC,North Dakota|ND,Ohio|OH,Oklahoma|OK,Oregon|OR,Pennsylvania|PA,Rhode Island|RI,South Carolina|SC,South Dakota|SD,Tennessee|TN,Texas|TX,Utah|UT,Vermont|VT,Virginia|VA,Washington|WA,West Virginia|WV,Wisconsin|WI,Wyoming|WY' | split: ','

    assign abbr = state
    for pair in pairs
      assign kv = pair | split: '|'
      if kv[0] == state
        assign abbr = kv[1]
        break
      endif
    endfor
  -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- liquid
  assign place = city
  if city != blank and abbr != blank
    assign place = city | append: ', ' | append: abbr
  elsif city == blank
    assign place = abbr
  endif
-%}
{{- place -}}
